    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35332" root="قذر" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذِرٌ</span></b> , (Lth, S, Mgh, Msb, K,) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذِرَ</span>, (Lth.)
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذْرٌ</span></b> , (Lth, K,) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذُرَ</span>, (Lth,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذُرٌ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَذَرٌ</span></b> , (K,) [but the last has an intensive signification, as though meaning “ dirt, ” or “ filth, ”
itself, (see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُرَّةٌ</span>,)] A thing <i>unclean, dirty,</i> or <i>filthy.</i>
(S, Mgh, Msb.)

